IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ma-types`
IMPORT `ma-schedules`

-- Metrication Act 1970 — GOAL 1: IS THIS UNIT PART OF THE INTERNATIONAL SYSTEM
-- OF UNITS, AND WHERE? and GOAL 2: DOES USING IT HAVE LEGAL FORCE?
--
-- ss 2, 3 and 7(2), with the First, Second and Fourth Schedules.
--
-- Source: ../source/MA1970.txt.

§ `Goals 1 and 2 — SI units and legal force`

§§ `Goal 1 — the unit's place in the International System of Units (ss 2, 3(2))`

-- s 2(1): "'International System of Units' — (a) means the metric system of
-- units as set out in the First and Second Schedules; and (b) includes the
-- units set out in the Fourth Schedule unless there is something in the
-- subject or context thereof inconsistent with such construction or unless
-- it is therein otherwise expressly provided." s 3(2) lists the same three.
-- Whether a written law's subject or context excludes the Fourth Schedule
-- units is a reading of that law: an input.
@ref Metrication Act 1970 ss 2(1), 3(2)
GIVEN u                                 IS A Unit
      `the context excludes the Fourth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a unit of the International System of Units:` u `, the context excluding the Fourth Schedule:` `the context excludes the Fourth Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the Schedule row for` u
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST row THEN CONSIDER row's `schedule`
                       WHEN `the First Schedule`  THEN TRUE                                               -- (a), s 3(2)(a)
                       WHEN `the Second Schedule` THEN TRUE                                               -- (a), s 3(2)(b)
                       WHEN `the Fourth Schedule` THEN NOT `the context excludes the Fourth Schedule`      -- (b), s 3(2)(c)
                       OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 2(2): "The abbreviation 'SI' is recognised as a legal reference to the
-- International System of Units."
@ref Metrication Act 1970 s 2(2)
GIVEN abbreviation IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a recognised legal reference to the International System of Units:` abbreviation IF
    abbreviation EQUALS "SI"


@ref ss 2(1), 3(2); First, Second and Fourth Schedules
GIVEN u                                         IS A Unit
      `the context excludes the Fourth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `SI status`
`the SI status of` u `, the context excluding the Fourth Schedule:` `the context excludes the Fourth Schedule` MEANS
    `SI status` WITH
        `a unit of the International System of Units` IS `a unit of the International System of Units:` u `, the context excluding the Fourth Schedule:` `the context excludes the Fourth Schedule`
        `role`     IS `the role`
        `symbol`   IS `the symbol`
        `quantity` IS `the quantity`
    WHERE
        `the symbol` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the Schedule row for` u
            WHEN JUST r  THEN JUST (r's `symbol`)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        `the quantity` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the Schedule row for` u
            WHEN JUST r  THEN JUST (r's `quantity`)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        `the role` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the Schedule row for` u
            WHEN NOTHING  THEN `not a unit of the International System`
            WHEN JUST row THEN CONSIDER row's `schedule`
                               WHEN `the First Schedule`  THEN `a basic unit`                                                -- s 3(2)(a)
                               WHEN `the Second Schedule` THEN `a supplementary or derived unit`                             -- s 3(2)(b)
                               WHEN `the Fourth Schedule` THEN IF `the context excludes the Fourth Schedule`
                                                               THEN `not a unit of the International System`
                                                               ELSE `a unit used in conjunction with them`                  -- s 3(2)(c)
                               OTHERWISE `not a unit of the International System`

§§ `Goal 2 — the legal force of using the unit (ss 3(1), 7(2))`

-- s 3(1): "On and after 15 February 1971, the use of the system of units
-- known as the International System of Units has legal force and validity in
-- Singapore." Before that day this Act gives it none — the Act's own answer.
@ref Metrication Act 1970 s 3(1)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use of SI has legal force and validity in Singapore under s 3(1) on` d IF
    d AT LEAST YMD 1971 2 15

-- s 7(2): "Nothing in this Act affects the legal force and validity of any
-- other system of units lawfully used in Singapore."
@ref Metrication Act 1970 s 7(2)
GIVEN `lawfully used in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act leaves another system's legal force untouched, it being lawfully used:` `lawfully used in Singapore` IF
    `lawfully used in Singapore`

-- The answer to Goal 2: the use of an SI unit on or after 15 February 1971 has
-- legal force and validity under s 3(1); the use of a unit of another system
-- that is lawfully used in Singapore keeps its force (s 7(2)), which this Act
-- neither gives nor takes away; otherwise the Act gives the use no force.
-- s 3(1) is not exclusive: an SI unit lawfully used before 1971 is also saved
-- by s 7(2).
@ref ss 3(1), 7(2)
GIVEN u                                          IS A Unit
      `the context excludes the Fourth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `used on`                                  IS A DATE
      `the use is lawful in Singapore under another system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Legal force of the use`
`the legal force of using` u `, the context excluding the Fourth Schedule:` `the context excludes the Fourth Schedule` `, on` `used on` `, lawful under another system:` `the use is lawful in Singapore under another system` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a unit of the International System of Units:` u `, the context excluding the Fourth Schedule:` `the context excludes the Fourth Schedule` AND `the use of SI has legal force and validity in Singapore under s 3(1) on` `used on`
              THEN `legal force and validity under s 3(1)`
           IF `the Act leaves another system's legal force untouched, it being lawfully used:` `the use is lawful in Singapore under another system`
              THEN `its own legal force, preserved by s 7(2)`
           OTHERWISE `no legal force from this Act`
